From 8e06549d6bc36cbaf01677436415223a4f5c9128 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 08:54:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] g4ants3: O(1) ants3 material index lookup by G4Material
 pointer

SessionManager::findMaterial(const std::string &) did a std::map
string lookup for every recorded step. It is replaced by an inline
findMaterial(const G4Material *), which reads the ants3 index from
G4IndexToAntsIndex[material->GetIndex()]. The vector is filled once at
the end of setupMaterials(). Unknown materials still terminate the
session with the same message.

Updated call sites: SensitiveDetector (deposition output),
SteppingAction and TrackingAction (tracking history), and the direct
deposition of the source generator. Output formats are unchanged: they
still contain the ants3 material index. With the dedicated Geant4
material per ants3 material from the previous commit, the index is now
also unambiguous for several materials based on the same NIST material.

MaterialMap is removed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
